{"authored" [{"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{7}}{7})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }[(-1)^{7}-{1}^{7}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $g(x)=2{x}^{3}-x-1$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{0-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x)|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(8-2+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-8x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(6{x}^{2}-8x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{3}-4{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ -12 & =2{c}^{2}-4c-10 \\\\ 0 & =2{c}^{2}-4c+2 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-2c+1 \\\\ 0 & =(c-1)^{2} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-20+80-10=50.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-8)}\\cdot (50) \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96373f1a5e646301ca30e8c4c47aa94c2b9defbffb6c1f3cd696083a3da744e3" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{25}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/state.json" "file_sha256" "dada277ed41e576f3b304a0b8072e1469be5b958dac7c11025a592599d08cd73" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-547.json" "file_sha256" "93b9658cd088ce20e1b393f27b3750dbdc4e6149f9fa47a6101f901de851ee0f" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-547.json" "file_sha256" "93b9658cd088ce20e1b393f27b3750dbdc4e6149f9fa47a6101f901de851ee0f" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-548.json" "file_sha256" "ea5755655871f1a8187caf2a4b73b29959c623f03dea5c558d1dfb3d9d6df9f5" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-548.json" "file_sha256" "ea5755655871f1a8187caf2a4b73b29959c623f03dea5c558d1dfb3d9d6df9f5" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-549.json" "file_sha256" "e8471e608ebd2f2949ac18d4e8f7bb738346837727553819394ea6445e2ea7cd" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-549.json" "file_sha256" "e8471e608ebd2f2949ac18d4e8f7bb738346837727553819394ea6445e2ea7cd" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-550.json" "file_sha256" "4304db3edff789dea900946efa14d54a32308786aca650fd325c6bb5568391b6" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/example-550.json" "file_sha256" "4304db3edff789dea900946efa14d54a32308786aca650fd325c6bb5568391b6" "basis" 1167 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7b92142725c210573acf7b23c225b00b3462387b68f80564e2919b6535ab704" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7b92142725c210573acf7b23c225b00b3462387b68f80564e2919b6535ab704" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19baef0445400a7097f3fcbdb2df1d8c65b1ade3eccfd42354331ae950c4fd4" "basis" 1983 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-120298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=6{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[-1,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (2{x}^{3})|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(2)^{3}-2(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =6 \\\\ 6{c}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =1 \\\\ c & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-120298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\pm 1"] ["math" "\\pm 6"] ["math" "\\pm \\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pm 1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=3{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[-2,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ({x}^{3})|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{2}^{3}-(-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4 \\\\ 3{c}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-2491" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2491" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}"] ["math" "\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2491" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=5\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}$ on the interval $[0,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2{x}^{5/2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\cdot {2}^{5/2}-2\\cdot {0}^{5/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{{c}^{3}} & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-120333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{25}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{25}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{16}{5}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=4+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ on the interval $[1,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(4+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(4x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}})-(4\\cdot 1-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{4}-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =\\frac{19}{4} \\\\ 4+\\frac{2}{{c}^{3}} & =\\frac{19}{4} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{c}^{3}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{c}^{3}}{2} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ {c}^{3} & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{8}{3}} \\\\ c & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-2476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt[3]{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=-x+2$ on the interval $[-2,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals. we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(-x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2x)|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+2\\cdot 2)-(-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}+2\\cdot (-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[2-(-6)] \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ -c+2 & =2 \\\\ c & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-2474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\pm 1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-2474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-2x$ on the interval $[-2,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-{x}^{2})|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {1}^{4}-{1}^{2})-(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-(-2)^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{3}{4}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-30771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30771" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $g(x)=2{x}^{3}-x-1$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{0-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x)|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(8-2+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A biologist found that the population $P$ of some bacteria in a petri dish can be modeled by the function $P(t)=200+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}t),$ where $t$ is the number of hours after $12$ noon. Find the average number of bacteria during the period from $12$ noon to $4$ p.m." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the function is valid starting from $12$ P.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,4].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}P(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-0}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(200+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}t))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}(200t-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\,t}{4}))|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(200\\cdot 4-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 4}{4}))-(200\\cdot 0-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{4}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(800-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(800-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))+\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\cdot 1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[800+\\frac{32}{\\pi }+\\frac{32}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(800+\\frac{64}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =200+\\frac{16}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-30903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "200+\\frac{16}{\\pi }"] ["math" "200-\\frac{12}{\\pi }"] ["math" "210-\\frac{1}{\\pi }"] ["math" "220+\\frac{5}{\\pi }"] ["math" "230-\\frac{2}{\\pi }"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "200+\\frac{16}{\\pi }"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{7}}{7})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }[(-1)^{7}-{1}^{7}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344648" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Within the interval $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ determine the average value of $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(0+(-1))-(0+1)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-30893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{3\\pi }"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\pi }"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-30893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order**, the **exact** nonzero values of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=12{x}^{2}-16x-12$ over the interval with endpoints $0$ and $c$ is equal to $0$ are\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and  $\\,c=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c\\ne 0,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(12{x}^{2}-16x-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}-12x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(4{c}^{3}-8{c}^{2}-12c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =4{c}^{2}-8c-12 \\\\ 0 & =4({c}^{2}-2c-3) \\\\ 0 & =4(c-3)(c+1) \\\\ c & =-1,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in **ascending order**, the values of $c$ are \n\n$$\nc=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,c=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-316306" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316306" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316306" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316306" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-3\\sqrt{x}$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-3\\sqrt{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -6 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3/2})|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3/2})-(0)] \\\\ -6 & =-2\\sqrt{c} \\\\ \\sqrt{c} & =3 \\\\ c & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-74069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-24x+23$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3{x}^{2}-24x+23)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}({x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+23x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[({c}^{3}-12{c}^{2}+23c)-0] \\\\ -12 & ={c}^{2}-12c+23 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-12c+35 \\\\ 0 & =(c-5)(c-7) \\\\ c & =5,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-74072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1,\\,4"] ["math" "2,\\,3"] ["math" "2,\\,7"] ["math" "3,\\,5"] ["math" "5,\\,7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5,\\,7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-9{x}^{2}+14x-2$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-9{x}^{2}+14x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-3{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-3{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-2c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-3{c}^{2}+7c-2 \\\\ 3{c}^{2}-7c+2 & =0 \\\\ (c-2)(3c-1) & =0 \\\\ c & =2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-120450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2,\\,3"] ["math" "-3,\\,2"] ["math" "0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-120450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-8x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(6{x}^{2}-8x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{3}-4{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ -12 & =2{c}^{2}-4c-10 \\\\ 0 & =2{c}^{2}-4c+2 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-2c+1 \\\\ 0 & =(c-1)^{2} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344596" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-18143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/7eddb6203ccc3eead9a2a89d7868d3206af52be4c269962e33c551ddd3cf08cd.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-4,4],$ is shown above. It consists of six line segments.  Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-1,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-18143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-(-1)}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-18143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-18143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-18143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-18143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/7ecbb53bb87156d11f9a9d8021182cdfb8c0c1749cd028780377bb61f32adf43.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-3,6]$, is shown above. It consists of the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(0,0)$ with radius $3,$ and two line segments. Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,5].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,3].$ The corresponding region is a semi-cirle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-(-3)}\\cdot (\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-74172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\pi }{8}+\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-74172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"] ["math" "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}"] ["math" "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-15225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-344702" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-20+80-10=50.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-8)}\\cdot (50) \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9a8e24c447fad0ceb1a846a0c2c85ca0fb9ff9d035ec865d16fb94c4ff19f71"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "q-316307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{25}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/state.json" "file_sha256" "cf12511ab2a241a59354fddd325ca3408cb0f58561780380803d1df83b677b56"} {"question" "e-547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-547.json" "file_sha256" "00c189854e380de03f631d78306c8098911c874c14b4e6d8e8d618ba9f618dad"} {"question" "e-547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-547.json" "file_sha256" "00c189854e380de03f631d78306c8098911c874c14b4e6d8e8d618ba9f618dad"} {"question" "e-548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-548.json" "file_sha256" "e246cf98b09467e2a41cb8fcaa8840e1f7aa715db96407dec6296e41a2d015fa"} {"question" "e-548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-548.json" "file_sha256" "e246cf98b09467e2a41cb8fcaa8840e1f7aa715db96407dec6296e41a2d015fa"} {"question" "e-549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-549.json" "file_sha256" "5b87974d3f11b7466a1f585875c6111ab2487e6310a7c3a148633cb2405c921a"} {"question" "e-549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-549.json" "file_sha256" "5b87974d3f11b7466a1f585875c6111ab2487e6310a7c3a148633cb2405c921a"} {"question" "e-550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-550.json" "file_sha256" "9fbaa490e86b62cb0ce1e799d5887542b04d6e43c6719ce8d7b37ee0cc86e7fe"} {"question" "e-550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/example-550.json" "file_sha256" "9fbaa490e86b62cb0ce1e799d5887542b04d6e43c6719ce8d7b37ee0cc86e7fe"}] "usage" {"q-15225" [] "q-30776" [] "e-548" [] "e-547" [] "q-316307" [] "q-344702" [] "e-550" [] "q-2491" [] "q-344648" [] "e-549" [] "q-344596" []} "basis" 2837 "retractions" [[17592186101252 :question/problem "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x) = 3x^{2}$ on the interval $[- 2, 2]$."] [17592186342308 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8